## H1 — Per-char OoStr concat (should be gone)
File: `/home/jeryd/Projects/openOODA/ooda/oodac/c_emit_secret_guard.oo`

Walker body (`c_guard_scan_idents`, L18–112):

- Linear index walk; ident start `_`/alpha, cont alnum/`_`.
- **One** extract: `let name = str_slice(args, start, i);` then `c_secret_refuse_sink_resolved`.
- Source has **zero** `name = name + c` / `out = out + char_at` inside this function.
- Header comment (L17): “Ident spans via str_slice once per token — no per-char OoStr thrash.”

Lowered C (`ooda/oodac/stage1_noarc.tmp.c` `void c_guard_scan_idents`):

| Primitive | Present? |
|-----------|----------|
| `oo_str_slice` | yes (once per ident) |
| `oo_str_concat` | **no** |
| `oo_char_at` | yes (cursor) |
| `char name[N]` / stack buf | **no** |
| `oo_str_release(name)` after refuse | yes |

Contrast (still OPEN elsewhere, not 7.1):

- `c_parse_secret_env` (`c_emit_secret.oo:60`) `name = name + c` — **7.10**
- `c_args_strip_cr` (`c_emit_args.oo:188`) `out = out + c` — CR strip, not 7.1

**H1: PASS.** The 7.1 concat leak is gone.

