## H2 — Quadratic walk on long args
### Mechanism (code, not slogan)
`oo_char_at` (`ooda/runtime/chs_rt_str.c`):

- `utf8_byte_index` rescans from byte 0 to `idx` every call.
- Always `malloc`s a 1-char `OoStr`.

Loop `i in 0..n` with `char_at(args, i)` ⇒ **Θ(n²) time** + n short-lived 1-char strings (ARC `oo_str_release` on the cursor in the lowered walker).

`oo_str_slice(args, start, i)` additionally calls `oo_chars_len(args)` (**O(n)**) on every ident, then two `utf8_byte_index` walks unless `end == n`.

`c_secret_refuse_sink_resolved` → `c_secret_resolve_alias` (≤16) → `c_env_get` (another `char_at` scan of `env`). Env is small on these fixtures.

Adjacent (not walker OWN): `c_emit_call_args` joins with `args = args + ", " + a` — classic concat of the **joined** text (O(n²) copies of the args string, still tiny vs lex).

### Measurements (cheap emit-c of generated fixtures)
Harness: ephemeral `/tmp/s71_mem_*` (not landed). `oodac emit-c` of:

- **idents_N** — `println(a0000, …)` N bare idents (hits full `c_guard_scan_idents`)
- **string_N** — `println("xxx…")` same arg-text length (string-skip walk, no slices)
- **mega_N** — one huge ident of same length (lex ident concat + **one** slice)

Isolated retimes (`/usr/bin/time` `%e` sec / `%M` maxrss KB; 2 trials, better shown):

| N | src B | idents sec | idents RSS KB | string sec | string RSS KB | mega sec | mega RSS KB |
|---|------:|-----------:|--------------:|-----------:|--------------:|---------:|------------:|
| 200 | ~1460 | 0.86 | 15800 | 0.40 | 7224 | 0.31 | 7560 |
| 400 | ~2860 | 1.28 | 27892 | 0.71 | 9948 | 0.57 | 10296 |
| 800 | ~5660 | 2.49 | 52324 | 1.81 | 15032 | 2.71 | 15928 |
| 1600 | ~11260 | 8.76 | 101236 | 7.06 | 25528 | 14.10 | 27528 |

Product fixtures (same binary):

| Fixture | src B | sec | maxrss KB | rc |
|---------|------:|----:|----------:|---:|
| `secret_sink_pass.oo` | 147 | 0.08 | 5104 | 0 |
| `secret_t2_args_println_ok_pass.oo` | 171 | 0.05 | 5176 | 0 |
| `hello.oo` | 583 | 0.11 | 7096 | 0 |
| tiny `println(1)` | 34 | 0.01 | 4572 | 0 |

**Read of the numbers:**

1. **idents RSS ≈ 63 KB · N** (15.8 → 27.9 → 52.3 → 101.2 MB). Linear in token/list emit, **not** quadratic heap from the walker.
2. **string / mega RSS** stay ~7–28 MB at the same source size — walker slice temps are not the RSS driver; token `List` + emit env are.
3. **Time** 800→1600 is ~3.3× (idents) / ~3.9× (string) / ~5.2× (mega) for 2× source. Superlinear, consistent with `char_at` + lex. mega is worst because **lex** still per-char-concats the huge IDENT (`token_scan_ident`) — that is **not** 7.1.
4. Extra cost of 1600 ident slices + refuse vs long-string skip: ~1.7 s and **+76 MB RSS** (token list), not a concat bomb.
5. Control `lets_N` (N `let` + `println(1)`) is a **different** emit thrash (env put / stmt list): N=400 was 110 s / 439 MB. Do not attribute that to `c_guard_scan_idents`.

**H2 heap: PASS.** **H2 time: residual** (same class as lex; 11 KiB fake args still finish; 64 KiB rail would be slow, not a new 7.1 leak).

