## Complexity (memory class)
| Function | Time | Aux heap |
|----------|------|----------|
| `c_guard_scan_idents` | Θ(\|args\|²) `char_at` + O(idents · \|env\|) refuse | O(1) scalars + O(\|ident\|) slice, released |
| `c_secret_refuse_sink_resolved` | O(1) alias hops ≤16 | O(1) |
| `c_emit_call_args` join | O(\|joined\|²) concat (adjacent) | growing `args` string once per call |

Progress: outer `i` always increases (by 1, 2, or ident length). No spin.

Minor generated-C residual: continuation loop `break`s **before** `oo_str_release(d)` on the first non-cont char ⇒ **1-char leak per ident** if ARC emit does not elide. At N=1600 that is KB-class, not the 7.1 concat bug.

