## Close bar for 7.1 (memory)
Path-A **may close 7.1 as memory-floor PASS** if process accepts:

1. Concat gone (proven here).
2. Slice ≡ the alpha “buffer” (proven here; matches `t1_memory.oot`).
3. `char_at` quadratic **time** stays a named residual (compiler-wide), not a 7.1 reopen.

Re-open 7.1 only if concat returns, or emit-c of ≤64 KiB args **OOMs** / RSS grows as Θ(n²) from the walker.

